Install imported files without a cross-filesystem rename

Android may back the app cache (getCacheDir) with a different filesystem than
the profile's folder. The import staged the checked file in the cache and moved
it into place with rename(), which the kernel refuses with EXDEV, so every
import on such a device failed with "Cross-device link" and installed nothing.

place() copies into a scratch file beside the destination and renames within
that one directory, so the install is atomic whatever the source filesystem is.
Free space is checked first, and a failed copy leaves neither the scratch file
nor a partial target behind.

Applied to kaito65452/horizon-android at 4681e5f (branch android); it applies
cleanly to a fresh clone of that commit.
